        """
}
mapping "b126.1" source="b126" target="SNOMED_CT:71565002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b126 SNOMED CT 71565002 (Temperament and personality functions) = ICF b126: mental functions
        of the person's enduring personality traits and temperament (extraversion b1260, openness,
        conscientiousness, etc.). Target (Athena 4324252) =, active standard, Swedish synonym. The
        SNOMED CT personality-function observable is the direct equivalent of the personality axis of ICF
        b126 and fully subsumes all b126 sub-functions (it sits under 3850002 311465003). Broader rather
        than exact: ICF b126 explicitly spans BOTH temperament AND personality, while the SNOMED CT concept
        names only personality (there is no dedicated SNOMED CT observable), so the target captures the
        personality axis and leaves the temperament axis implicit. High tier : strong term +
        Swedish-synonym match and verified crosswalk; one-level-broader because temperament is not
        separately modelled.
        """
}
mapping "b1260.1" source="b1260" target="SNOMED_CT:286692009" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1260 SNOMED CT 286692009 = ICF b1260: extraversion specifically — a personality trait, the
        degree to which a person is outward-oriented/sociable. Target (Athena 4113478) =, active
        standard, Swedish synonym (degree of extraversion). The SNOMED CT concept is the only standard
        concept that names extraversion; its Swedish synonym directly matches the source. Related rather
        than exact/narrower: ICF b1260 models extraversion as a personality FUNCTION (a body-function
        construct), whereas models it as a LEVEL/observable (a measurable degree). These are the same
        construct in different modelling paradigms — the level-of-extraversion observable is clinically
        associated with and the closest standard representation of the extraversion function, but it is
        not a function concept, so it is a related link. Moderate-to-low tier : tight, defensible
        association with a direct Swedish-synonym match, capped below broader because the paradigm gap
        (function vs level/observable) is real.
        """
}
